module gunbc.rung_drop.determinism_transitive_reachability

import std.types { NonEmptyStr, List }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { GuaranteeRung, MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }

// RUNG DROP — DETERMINISM TRANSITIVE REACHABILITY (2026-09-05).
//
// The fn-arrow corpus_dependency_view composition (mechanism #2 of the §3 consolidation)
// carried fn-arrow declarations across ~25 lens modules whose call graph the
// determinism_transitive_holds witness walked. Deleting corpus_dependency_view removed
// those declarations' subject modules from the fn_arrow_decl_facts_live acquisition
// (they were under src/v2/lens/affected_set, which also contained the deleted modules).
// As a result, determinism_transitive_live_closure_holds can no longer follow callee
// edges into other modules within budget.
//
// The witness has been renamed to determinism_live_intra_holds to reflect that only
// intra-declaration determinism is checked. No cross-module callee traversal occurs.
// This is a real check of each declaration's own structure but does NOT establish
// that the call graph is determinism-safe.
//
// CAUSE CORRECTED BY MEASUREMENT, 2026-09-07. This row previously attributed the budget
// pressure to the NUMBER OF REACHABLE DECLARATIONS, and that attribution is refuted rather
// than refined: the directory-grain walk this drop is gated on reaches FEWER THAN A HUNDRED
// declarations -- barely more than the 78 it seeds from -- and still costs many times the
// per-claim line. The cost is not in the reached set. The wrong sentence was replaced rather
// than annotated, because a restoration trigger is the whole check: a trigger naming a term
// that is not the cost is satisfied by nothing, and it would stand forever with an
// honest-looking receipt attached while anyone chasing it optimised a quantity that does not
// move the number.
//
// AND THE REPLACEMENT SENTENCE WAS ITSELF REFUTED, 2026-09-07, BY THE FIRST LANE THAT TRIED TO
// SATISFY IT. Only the irreducible reasoning is kept here; the executed evidence, the instrument
// that re-derives it, and the prescription all live in `restoration_trigger` below, because a
// second copy of them beside the field would be the fork this row exists to prevent.
//
// WHY A TRIGGER IS WITHDRAWN RATHER THAN WEAKENED. A restoration trigger is a repair
// PRESCRIPTION, not a note. Once the mechanism it was derived from is false, leaving it standing
// as the declared way out with a "that repair did not help" remark beside it is worse than
// deleting it: the next reader follows the prescription, not the remark. So the prescription is
// removed and nothing replaces it until the cost is attributed to a construct that executes.
//
// WHY A CORRECT FIT CARRYING A FALSE MECHANISM IS THE DANGEROUS ARTIFACT, and the reason this row
// has now been corrected twice. A fit that survives its tests looks like a diagnosis, so the
// mechanism sentence beside it is read as established rather than as the hypothesis it is -- and
// every repair it recruits is aimed at a construct nobody measured. That is not hypothetical here:
// it recruited gunbc#10753, which built the prescribed repair, measured it, and found it worse
// than what it replaced. The fit and the mechanism are therefore carried as SEPARATE claims with
// separate standing, and this row states which is which.
//
// WHY THE NUMBERS ARE NOT WRITTEN DOWN HERE. DESIGN §6 -- name the instrument, never transcribe
// its output. The lane that wrote this correction transcribed a full result table into the field
// below on its first attempt, which would have reproduced, one layer up, exactly the failure this
// row records: a pile of figures unreachable from the thing that owns them, rotting without
// anyone touching either end, while the recipe to re-derive them had been deleted to make room.

// ONE OBSERVATION, AT THE GRAIN IT WAS TAKEN AND NO WIDER. Under claim_batch on a BuildBuddy
// runner the directory-grain walk EXECUTES, COMPLETES AND PASSES at 6-7 seconds -- it is not
// interrupted there. That establishes executability and says NOTHING about the required floor,
// whose disposition for this claim is unpinned and where whether a poll-visible deadline is
// armed the same way is unresolved. AND `interrupted_before_verdict` IS A DISPOSITION SHARED
// ACROSS UNRELATED SUBJECTS, NOT A NAME FOR THIS POPULATION: the same cause appears on main-tip
// floor receipts for outside_modeled_guarantee_witness_test and for
// test.claim.long.carrier_reference_integrity_witness_test, which have nothing to do with this
// walk. A reader must not infer from the cause alone that it describes one subject.
//
// AND THE WITNESS BLOCKS INTERMITTENTLY, WHICH IS THE WORD THAT SURVIVED TWO WRONG ONES. On main
// tip 9b341e1b03 it appears once, in a roster membership list, and NOT on a BLOCKING line; on
// gunbc#10764 -- a pull request of eight lines of Rust comment, touching no .dag at all -- it
// BLOCKS, cause `interrupted_before_verdict`, adjudication REFUSED. Both observations are true, so
// neither "resolved" nor "steadily blocking" is the fact: it is INTERMITTENT, and because #10764
// changes nothing this row reads, the intermittency is a property of MAIN rather than of any
// branch.
//
// THE READING ERROR IS RECORDED BECAUSE IT WAS MADE TWICE IN ONE NIGHT, in both directions, by
// people watching this row: a single green tip was taken as the class being resolved, and a single
// red as it being steady. One tip is one sample of an intermittent process, and consecutive main
// tips are not a controlled comparison -- they differ by whatever else landed. NEITHER OBSERVATION
// IS A COST MEASUREMENT and neither is recorded as one; a witness can stop or start blocking
// because it got cheaper, because the accounting changed, or because something upstream moved.
//
// AN INTERMITTENT BLOCKER IS WORSE THAN A STEADY ONE, WHICH IS WHY THE ATTRIBUTION IS URGENT AND
// NOT A BACKLOG ITEM. A deterministic red gets fixed; a coin-flip red gets rerun, every rerun is a
// full floor job, and the cost is paid by authors of unrelated lanes who have no way to know the
// red is not theirs -- a red on your own PR looks like yours. That is the deferred-cost shape
// DESIGN §1 names: the principal paying is not the one who caused it.
//
// So this row's `interrupted_before_verdict` cause is recorded
// as UNVERIFIED PENDING REQUIRED-FLOOR INSTRUMENTATION: not "cannot finish", and equally not
// "finishes over budget on the floor", because the run that would license the second sentence
// has not been taken.
data determinism_transitive_reachability: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "determinism_transitive_reachability" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Transitive determinism reachability over the fn-arrow call graph",

  declared: "2026-09-05",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: [
      "v2.lens.affected_set.corpus_dependency_view (fn-arrow composition, deleted)",
      "v2.lens.affected_set.entry_selection (fn-arrow declarations, deleted)",
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "CAPABILITY WITHDRAWN, NOT WEAKENED, 2026-09-07 -- THIS ROW PRESCRIBES NO REPAIR UNTIL THE COST IS ATTRIBUTED TO A CONSTRUCT THAT EXECUTES. The previously declared capability (the callee lookup answering BY INDEX rather than by scanning the candidate pool) is withdrawn because the mechanism it was derived from is refuted by execution. THE REFUTATION, BY REASONING: v2.std.fn_index.decls_in_modules is a plain-valued call with hashable arguments, and the v1 interpreter's eval-frame call memo is on by default (GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO), keyed by fn identity x argument identity -- so the loop-invariant that trigger asked a lane to hoist had already been hoisted by the interpreter, and the per-lookup rescan named as the cost was not being paid. THE REFUTATION, BY MEASUREMENT: gunbc#10753 built exactly the prescribed index and measured it against the unindexed lookup at directory grain under a verdict rule pre-registered before the numbers existed; that PR carries the method, the pre-registration and the figures, and is the citation for them rather than a copy here. Its verdict is that the index is HARMFUL -- it adds cost and removes none -- and that both arms remain far above the per-claim line, so the prescription was not merely insufficient but wrong. WHAT SURVIVES: the O(reached x pool) FIT, unchanged and still good evidence. WHAT DOES NOT: the causal sentence behind it. ATTRIBUTION SO FAR, RE-DERIVED BY NAMING ITS INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN ITS OUTPUT -- run test.claim.fn_index_attribution_probe (scratch-probe/test/claim/fn_index_attribution_probe.dag) under claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root scratch-probe, whose six arms separate acquisition, the closure list, the reachability walk, and the walk plus the determinism fold, and whose last two arms hold the entry and the CLOSURE fixed while enlarging only the candidate POOL so the reached set is unchanged. THE CITATION IS A POINTER AND NOT A GUARANTEE, AND THE EXPOSURE IS STATED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT FOR A READER TO DISCOVER. scratch-probe/ is reached by no source root, no scan dir and no row other than this one, so that module is OUTSIDE EVERY COMPILED CLOSURE: a renamed builtin, a changed signature or a moved module would rot the instrument with NO RED ANYWHERE, and this row would then cite an instrument that does not run, which is the failure naming an instrument exists to prevent. WHY IT IS NOT HOMED WHERE A COMPILE WOULD CATCH THAT, CORRECTED 2026-09-07 (gunbc#10757, review 61911): the argument this row carried until now was that enrolling the probe would put six multi-second claims on the required floor, and that argument was WRONG BECAUSE IT ANSWERED A DIFFERENT QUESTION -- the cost of RUNNING the arms is not the cost of COMPILING them, and a compile-only enrolment would buy the typecheck without running anything. The real reason is narrower and is a boundary rather than a trade: the compile-only surface is gunbc.ci_layer_roots.compile_clean_source_roots, and a root added there must also be added to the partition that dag_compile_clean_shard_a_witness_test.compile_clean_partition_boundary_matches_compile_clean_source_roots checks against it. That is a roster edit that widens what four serial full-corpus compiles cover on EVERY push and pull request, which this repository holds closed to growth without operator sign-off, and which the brief this lane works under forbids outright. So the exposure is not accepted as a good trade -- it is accepted as the residue of a discharge THIS LANE MAY NOT PERFORM, and the discharge remains available to whoever may: add 'scratch-probe' to compile_clean_source_roots and to that partition, and this whole paragraph dissolves. THE PROBE'S OWN DISSOLUTION, so this instrument does not outlive the question it was built for: scratch-probe/test/claim/fn_index_attribution_probe.dag exists ONLY to attribute the cost this row leaves unattributed, and the lane that either retires this row or names the pool-proportional construct DELETES that module in the same change. An instrument that survives its investigation is residue, and this one is not exempt because it is cited here. WHAT WOULD DETECT THE ROT: running it, which the next lane to take up the attribution trigger must do before quoting anything from it -- and partially, the fact that the probe imports ordinary std and lens symbols, so a rename broad enough to break it would usually break compiled consumers too. Partial, and not to be relied on. A LANE THAT FINDS THE INSTRUMENT ROTTED MUST REPAIR IT BEFORE READING THIS ROW'S FINDINGS, because those findings are only as live as the thing that re-derives them. What it establishes: the determinism fold is NOT the cost -- adding determinism_findings over every reached declaration's whole subtree does not rise above run-to-run noise, so a lane optimising it or its concat accumulator will move nothing; and the reachability WALK is pool-sensitive at a fixed reached set, which corroborates the pool term and locates it inside the walk. WHAT REMAINS UNATTRIBUTED, and is the next trigger: WHICH construct inside that walk is pool-proportional, given that the per-lookup rescan is refuted. One candidate a reader should not skip is the eval-frame memo's own keying, which must derive a key from the pool-sized argument on every call -- so a provider that removes a pool-sized scan can reintroduce a pool-sized cost in its key. That is a hypothesis and is not to be prescribed as a repair. A re-deriver must also pin whether each arm re-pays its acquisition or is served from a cross-witness share, which the probe does not settle. Only once the construct is named may this row name a repair, and the repair it names must be derived from that attribution. SUFFICIENT FOR (unchanged, and still the thing being restored): determinism_transitive_holds with pool_roots=['src/v2/lens'] and pool_files=[] reaching a verdict within the per-claim line at directory grain, WITHOUT NARROWING THE SUBJECT -- scoping pool_roots to the modules the walk happens to reach remains the trap and not the repair, because it lowers the number by shrinking the population, leaves the cost shape intact, and re-breaks the moment the subject widens, which is the widening this drop exists to restore. THREE COST SHAPES IN THIS WALK ARE REAL AND ARE MEASURED NOT TO BE THE COST, recorded so a later reader does not fix them and believe the defect is gone: call_reachable_decls_go scans `reached` linearly per seed (decl_in_list), appends with a copied accumulator (list_snoc_item), and list_append(rest, callee_decls) copies the seed list per step; determinism_transitive_findings folds with concat(acc, determinism_findings(...)), free while the corpus is clean and quadratic exactly when findings appear, so it is invisible in every green run; determinism_live_closure_modules folds list_snoc_item over a list that is empty today. Until the construct is attributed, determinism over the fn-arrow call graph is unverified and this row states no way out.",
  }
}
